You're fine for the part of the game you're in, in my experience. 
Onward and downward!  I'd avoid the alignment quests until later,
however, because Vecna, Nightmare and the Beholder are extremely
strong.  I suggest you stick to the Dungeon of Doom until you reach a
level where you start seeing monsters that make you a tad nervous -
probably around 25ish would be as far as you want to go at this point.
 Once that's done, go back up and start doing the side levels (Grund's
Stronghold, etc.  You probably want to duck into each as you find them
to generate the monsters inside at a lower level).  Just keep
improving your AC and you should be fine.  My Valkyrie has never nurse
danced, has only a bit shy of 200 hp, and has only had problems with
Demogorgon so far because of a -49 AC.

Good luck.  Be careful with rubber chickens.

